parameters.inputSchema:
={
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "topic": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The approved communication topic received from the upstream communication strategy."
    },
    "platforms": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "The exact target platforms received from the input request. Never hardcode, add, remove, or assume platforms.",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "minItems": 1
    },
    "media": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The approved media object for the downstream media workflow. Preserve the media decision and existing media information from upstream. Do not create a different media structure.",
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The approved media type.",
          "enum": [
            "image",
            "video",
            "none"
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "Existing user-provided or previously generated media URL. Null when no existing media URL is available."
        },
        "source": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "The origin of the media.",
          "enum": [
            "user",
            "generated",
            null
          ]
        },
        "generate": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "Whether downstream workflow nodes must generate the approved media."
        },
        "prompt": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "The approved media-generation prompt when media generation is required. Null when generation is not required."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "url",
        "source",
        "generate",
        "prompt"
      ]
    },
    "posts": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Exactly one platform-native content item for every platform present in the platforms array. Never hardcode, add, remove, or assume platforms.",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "platform": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The exact platform name from the input platforms array."
          },
          "headline": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "A platform-specific headline when appropriate. Return an empty string when the platform does not use a separate headline."
          },
          "caption": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Final platform-native content derived from the communication strategy, research, user instructions, business context, and platform conventions. Adapt the writing style, structure, formatting, audience behavior, and appropriate content length for the specific platform."
          },
          "hashtags": {
            "type": "array",
            "description": "Platform-appropriate hashtags. Return an empty array when hashtags are not appropriate for the platform or content.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "platform",
          "headline",
          "caption",
          "hashtags"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "topic",
    "platforms",
    "media",
    "posts"
  ]
}

parameters.text:
=Original User Request:

{{
  (() => {
    const q = $("When Executed by Another Workflow").first().json.query;
    return JSON.stringify(
      typeof q === "string" ? JSON.parse(q) : q,
      null,
      2
    );
  })()
}}

Communication Strategy:

{{ JSON.stringify($json.output || {}, null, 2) }}

Generate the final platform-specific content package using the original request and communication strategy.

Create content ONLY for the platforms explicitly requested by the user.

Every platform must have independently written, platform-native content. Do not copy, shorten, or mechanically rewrite one post across platforms.

Respect platform-specific content length, formatting, audience behavior, hook style, narrative structure, CTA behavior, and hashtag conventions.

Media is handled by the existing downstream media workflow. Return ONE overall media strategy/prompt for the package rather than creating separate media prompts for every platform.
